# HARD RULE: docs + ai-knowledge every iteration

Treat `@eristack/ai-knowledge` as a **required deliverable** of every incremental change — same priority as package docs. Do not ship code/docs without updating agent knowledge in the same pass.

## When this applies

Any non-trivial change to a publishable `@eristack/*` package (or adding one under `packages/<category>/`), including:

- APIs, defaults, adapters, persistence (e.g. Drizzle-first)
- Behavior agents must follow
- Docs, Intent skills, public exports, package description/version agents see
- New discoverable product language (“stock”, “FIFO”, “login”, …)

Trivial typo-only edits with **no** behavioral/API/guidance change may skip recipes — still run `pnpm knowledge:check` if you touched skills or package.json fields the catalog reads.

## Required every iteration (same change set)

1. **Package docs** — update `packages/<category>/<name>/docs/` (not chat-only, not `_ai-docs` alone).
2. **Intent skills** — update `packages/<category>/<name>/skills/**/SKILL.md` when guidance/defaults/APIs change.
3. **Recipes** — add/update `packages/ai/ai-knowledge/knowledge/recipes.yaml` when the capability should be found by product language (`recommend()`). New packages need a primary recipe unless they are pure internals with no user-facing ask (still catalogued via sync).
4. **Sync** — run `pnpm knowledge:sync`, then confirm `pnpm knowledge:check` passes.
5. **WIP notes** — if using `_ai-docs/<topic>/`, note what catalog/recipe/skill changed so promotion stays complete.

## Do not

- Finish an iteration with fresh docs but stale skills/recipes/catalog
- Hand-edit `packages/ai/ai-knowledge/src/generated/*` or the `<!-- catalog:* -->` block in `skills/recommend-eristack/SKILL.md`
- Defer knowledge sync to “later” / a follow-up PR unless the human explicitly scopes that out
- Present memory/test-only stores as the default in skills or recipes (Drizzle/DB-first)

## Definition of done (agent)

Code works **and** docs updated **and** skills/recipes reflect the change **and** `pnpm knowledge:check` is green **and** (when exports/build changed) `pnpm exports:check` is green after `pnpm build`.

## Documentation quality (HARD RULE — token budget)

See `.cursor/rules/docs-depth-tokens.mdc`. Cross-cutting topics = **one canonical** `knowledge/<topic>.md` (+ site mirror). Per-package docs = unique deltas only. Agents must finish upgrade/integration tasks in **≤3 files**, not by reading every package doc.
